   "date": "2014-09-10T18:52:23Z",
   "subject": "Unexpected packrat internet request?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">When starting the R console in a &quot;packrat&quot;ed directory, I observe unexpected internet requests.  They are detectable, because R is asking me for proxy information.<br><br>For example, bellow is what I do/see in the R console (the commented lines are me describing whats going on):<br><br><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">Packrat mode on. Using library in directory:<br>- &quot;C:/Users/erickjp/Documents/Stuff/PoolNSpa/PnS-Calculator/packrat/lib&quot;<br>&gt; a &lt;- 1<br><i>#  R pops open a &quot;Proxy authentication&quot;, I click Cancel.</i><br>&gt; b &lt;- 2<br>&gt; c &lt;- 3<br><i>#  R pops open a &quot;Proxy authentication&quot;, I click Cancel.</i><br>&gt; d &lt;- 4<br>&gt; e &lt;- 5<br><i>#  R pops open a &quot;Proxy authentication&quot;, I click Cancel.</i><br>&gt; </span><br><br>Does packrat really behind the scenes make internet requests?  I&#39;ve only observed this when packrat has been enabled.<br><br>Below is my sessionInfo:<br><br><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">&gt; sessionInfo()<br>R version 3.1.1 (2014-07-10)<br>Platform: x86_64-w64-mingw32/x64 (64-bit)<br><br>locale:<br>[1] LC_COLLATE=English_United States.1252 <br>[2] LC_CTYPE=English_United States.1252   <br>[3] LC_MONETARY=English_United States.1252<br>[4] LC_NUMERIC=C                          <br>[5] LC_TIME=English_United States.1252    <br><br>attached base packages:<br>[1] stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datasets  methods   base     <br><br>loaded via a namespace (and not attached):<br>[1] packrat_0.4.0.10 tools_3.1.1    </span><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "9A53kdD0EPsJ",
   "from": "Kevin Ushey",
   "author": "ab0d2be2ea8dabe8",
   "date": "2014-09-11T21:59:05Z",
   "subject": "Re: Unexpected packrat internet request?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Hi Joe,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Behind the scenes, packrat will do automatic snapshots — but this should not be making any internet requests.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Can you see if the behaviour disappears if you type <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat::opts$auto.snapshot(FALSE)</code>? It could be the automatic snapshot machinery running behind the scenes doing something it shouldn’t. Similarly, do you see the same message if you manually perform a snapshot (<code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat::snapshot()</code>)?</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Thanks,<br>Kevin</p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">On Wednesday, September 10, 2014 11:52:23 AM UTC-7, Joe Erickson wrote:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\"></p><div><p></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">When starting the R console in a &quot;packrat&quot;ed directory, I observe unexpected internet requests.  They are detectable, because R is asking me for proxy information.<br><br>For example, bellow is what I do/see in the R console (the commented lines are me describing whats going on):<br><br><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">Packrat mode on. Using library in directory:<br>- &quot;C:/Users/erickjp/Documents/Stuff/PoolNSpa/PnS-Calculator/packrat/lib&quot;<br>&gt; a &lt;- 1<br><i>#  R pops open a &quot;Proxy authentication&quot;, I click Cancel.</i><br>&gt; b &lt;- 2<br>&gt; c &lt;- 3<br><i>#  R pops open a &quot;Proxy authentication&quot;, I click Cancel.</i><br>&gt; d &lt;- 4<br>&gt; e &lt;- 5<br><i>#  R pops open a &quot;Proxy authentication&quot;, I click Cancel.</i><br>&gt; </span><br><br>Does packrat really behind the scenes make internet requests?  I&#39;ve only observed this when packrat has been enabled.<br><br>Below is my sessionInfo:<br><br><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">&gt; sessionInfo()<br>R version 3.1.1 (2014-07-10)<br>Platform: x86_64-w64-mingw32/x64 (64-bit)<br><br>locale:<br>[1] LC_COLLATE=English_United States.1252 <br>[2] LC_CTYPE=English_United States.1252   <br>[3] LC_MONETARY=English_United States.1252<br>[4] LC_NUMERIC=C                          <br>[5] LC_TIME=English_United States.1252    <br><br>attached base packages:<br>[1] stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datasets  methods   base     <br><br>loaded via a namespace (and not attached):<br>[1] packrat_0.4.0.10 tools_3.1.1    </span><br></div></blockquote><p></p></div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\"></p>\r