  {
   "id": "t3_sRA2ypJcJ",
   "from": "Kevin Ushey",
   "author": "ab0d2be2ea8dabe8",
   "date": "2014-09-15T17:04:48Z",
   "subject": "Re: Unexpected packrat internet request?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Joe,<div><br></div><div>I just pushed some code to packrat master that should alleviate this issue: <a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/packrat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/packrat&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242773090000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3s0Y_g1i-Wq7qdtj9_PDjq\">https://github.com/rstudio/packrat</a> -- by default, packrat will re-use the cached `available.packages()` (so you should only see the &#39;proxy&#39; request once per session, when the first call out to CRAN is made).<br><br>Thanks,<br>Kevin</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Sep 15, 2014 at 9:16 AM, Kevin Ushey <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ke...@rstudio.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Hi Joe,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">I think I know what’s happening. The automatic snapshot mechanism that packrat uses attempts to do automatic snapshots behind the scenes (ie, after every command entered by a user). This call involves a call to <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">available.packages()</code> at some point in the routine, which forces an internet request to CRAN (we ask CRAN for some dependency information on installed packages). I am guessing that this is tripping your proxy.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">In a regular R session, the information would be cached per-session — so the first time you call <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">available.packages()</code> I would expect the proxy pop-up; any subsequent calls in the same session should use the cached information. The problem with the automatic snapshot — we actually spawn a new R process to perform the snapshot, and this current doesn’t use the cached <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">available.packages()</code> information — hence necessitating an internet request on every expression.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">I would recommend keeping <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">opts$auto.snapshot(FALSE)</code> for now; and I will try to produce the appropriate fix for packrat soon as well.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Thanks,<br>Kevin</p><div><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">On Monday, September 15, 2014 7:48:12 AM UTC-7, Joe Erickson wrote:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\"></p><div><p></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">As you said.  When I enter<code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat::opts$auto.<u></u>snapshot(FALSE)</code>, the proxy pop-ups disappear for normal commands like <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">a &lt;- 3</code>.<br><br>Interestingly, when <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat::opts$auto.snapshot(<u></u>TRUE)</code>, <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat::snapshot()</code> produces a proxy pop-up each time it is entered.<br><br>However, when<code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat::opts$auto.<u></u>snapshot(FALSE)</code>, <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat::snapshot()</code>only produced a proxy pop-up the first time it was entered.  (not subsequent times)<br><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"><i><br></i></span><br><br></div></blockquote><p></p></div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\"></p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:SGkgSm9lLDxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+SSB0aGluayBJIGtub3cgd2hhdCdzIGhhcHBlbmlu\r\nZy4gVGhlIGF1dG9tYXRpYyBzbmFwc2hvdCBtZWNoYW5pc20gdGhhdCBwYWN